#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:13
msgid "Audit event"
msgstr "Événement d'audit"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:4
msgid "Deciding the request: the pilgrim's consents are the policy"
msgstr "Décider de la requête : les consentements du pèlerin constituent la politique"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the {code0} and {code1} of each Consent read from the Consent Registry for the decision;"
msgstr "les {code0} et {code1} de chaque Consent lus dans le Consent Registry pour la décision ;"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:19
msgid "the documents released (the DocumentReferences returned), or the refusal."
msgstr "les documents communiqués (les DocumentReferences renvoyées), ou le refus."

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:11
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The Host Country EMR is identified by trust in the {code0} trust domain (see the authentication note in the message semantics). The Origin Country HIE releases the documents only when the passcode is valid, the VHL has not expired, the origin-release consent is active in its registry, the verified receiver matches {code1}, the purpose is treatment, and the request falls within {code2}. If any of these cannot be established, the request is not permitted."
msgstr "Le DME du pays d'accueil est identifié par la confiance dans le domaine de confiance {code0} (voir la note sur l'authentification dans la sémantique des messages). La HIE du pays d'origine ne communique les documents que lorsque le code d'accès est valide, que le VHL n'a pas expiré, que le consentement à la communication par le pays d'origine est actif dans son registre, que le destinataire vérifié correspond à {code1}, que la finalité est le traitement et que la requête s'inscrit dans {code2}. Si l'une de ces conditions ne peut être établie, la requête n'est pas autorisée."

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:14
msgid "The Origin Country HIE records an audit event with Record Audit Event [ITI-20] for each request, whether documents are released or refused. VHL Volume 1 §1:XX.3 requires the VHL Sharer and the VHL Receiver to be grouped with an ATNA Secure Node or Secure Application, and ITI-YY5 §2:3.YY5.5.6 says both SHOULD log document access requests, the authentication method used, the receiver identity, the VHL folder ID and the authorization decision. In this guide the audit event recorded by the Origin Country HIE shall also cite:"
msgstr "La HIE du pays d'origine enregistre un événement d'audit avec Record Audit Event [ITI-20] pour chaque requête, que les documents soient communiqués ou refusés. Le volume 1 du VHL, §1:XX.3, exige que le VHL Sharer et le VHL Receiver soient groupés avec un ATNA Secure Node ou Secure Application, et ITI-YY5 §2:3.YY5.5.6 indique que tous deux DEVRAIENT journaliser les requêtes d'accès aux documents, la méthode d'authentification utilisée, l'identité du destinataire, l'identifiant du dossier VHL et la décision d'autorisation. Dans ce guide, l'événement d'audit enregistré par la HIE du pays d'origine doit également citer :"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:18
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the purpose of use ({code0});"
msgstr "la finalité d'utilisation ({code0}) ;"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:17
msgid "the receiver, as identified by the VHL authentication option used;"
msgstr "le destinataire, tel qu'identifié par l'option d'authentification VHL utilisée ;"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:2
msgid "The recipient OCHIE acts as a VHL Document Responder and must conform with the capability statement for <a0>VHL Document Responder</a0>"
msgstr "L'OCHIE destinataire agit en tant que VHL Document Responder et doit se conformer à la déclaration de capacités du <a0>VHL Document Responder</a0>"

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:1
msgid "The recipient OCHIE checks if the VHL request is valid and responds with the documentReference as a FHIR bundle Json."
msgstr "L'OCHIE destinataire vérifie si la requête VHL est valide et répond avec la documentReference sous la forme d'un bundle FHIR en JSON."

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Which consent a {code0} is, and the consent text the pilgrim was shown, are carried in {code1}: a code from the <a0>IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT</a0> CodeSystem, with {code2} set to the CodeSystem version."
msgstr "Le type de consentement que représente un {code0}, et le texte du consentement présenté au pèlerin, figurent dans {code1} : un code du CodeSystem <a0>IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT</a0>, avec {code2} défini sur la version du CodeSystem."

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:5
msgid "For the pilgrimage there is no separate data sharing agreement to look up. The pilgrim's two <a0>HajjConsent</a0> resources are the policy, and each one binds the party it names:"
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the governing policy: the pilgrim's consents, each by its {code0} code and CodeSystem version (for example {code1} and {code2} in this guide's examples, version 2.1.0);"
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The host-use consent ({code0}, or the fictional {code1} of this guide's examples) governs the Host Country Ministry of Health's use of the IPS after it is received: for treatment during the pilgrimage and any follow-up care, as its consent text states."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:6
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The origin-release consent (for example {code0}, or the fictional {code1} of this guide's examples) lets the Origin Country HIE release the IPS to the recipient named in {code2} (role {code3}, information recipient), for the purpose in {code4} ({code5}), during {code6}. The Origin Country HIE enforces this consent from its own Consent Registry (as recorded by the Record Consent transaction, [ITI-108]), not from the copy carried inside the IPS. The IPS copy is signed when the IPS is issued, so it cannot show a later withdrawal."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/transaction-retrieve-MHD-folder-request-expected-actions-semantics.md:21
msgid "This guide uses no separate data sharing agreement for the pilgrimage, so the consents themselves are the policy the audit event cites. The Host Country EMR, as an ATNA Secure Node or Secure Application, should also audit what it receives."
msgstr ""

